  "recommendation": "Add /guides/ hub to organize strategy guides and improve internal linking. Build 'Two Letter Scrabble Words' and 'Words Without Vowels' as new support pages.",
  "new_pages": [
    {
      "title": "Two Letter Scrabble Words",
      "slug": "two-letter-scrabble-words",
      "h1": "Two Letter Scrabble Words",
      "meta_description": "Complete list of two-letter Scrabble words, including official TWL and SOWPODS. Learn which are valid, how to use them, and common pitfalls.",
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "What Are Two Letter Scrabble Words?",
          "content": "Two-letter words are essential in Scrabble for parallel plays, hooks, and clearing tiles. Official word lists vary by region: TWL (North America) and SOWPODS (international)."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Official Two Letter Scrabble Words List",
          "content": "Below is the complete list of 107 two-letter words accepted in TWL (and 124 in SOWPODS). Note that some words like 'qi' are valid in TWL but not in all dictionaries. Always check tournament rules."
        },
        {
          "heading": "How to Memorize Two Letter Scrabble Words",
          "content": "Group by vowel patterns, use mnemonics, or practice with flashcards. Focus on high-value letters like Q, Z, and J (e.g., qi, za, jo)."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Common Mistakes with Two Letter Words",
          "content": "Avoid invalid words like 'ew' or 'ow' (not in TWL). Remember that 'aa' is valid in SOWPODS but not TWL. Always verify with official sources."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Words Without Vowels",
      "slug": "words-without-vowels",
      "h1": "Words Without Vowels",
      "meta_description": "List of English words with no vowels (A, E, I, O, U). Includes Scrabble-valid words, rare terms, and tips for word games.",
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "What Are Words Without Vowels?",
          "content": "Words without vowels use only consonants, often including 'y' as a vowel substitute. Examples: 'myth', 'lynx', 'crypt'. In Scrabble, words like 'hmm' and 'shh' are valid."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Complete List of Vowel-less Words",
          "content": "Common words: by, cry, dry, fly, fry, gym, hymn, lynx, myth, nymph, pyx, rhythm, shy, sky, sly, spy, sty, sync, thy, try, why, wry. Note: 'y' is considered a vowel in these contexts."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Using Vowel-less Words in Scrabble",
          "content": "These words are valuable for dumping consonants. However, many are short (2-4 letters). Longer words like 'rhythms' (7 letters) are rare. Check official lists for validity."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Words Without Vowels in Other Word Games",
          "content": "In Wordle, vowel-less words are uncommon but possible (e.g., 'myths'). In cryptograms, they often indicate 'y' as a vowel. In Boggle, they can be high-scoring if placed well."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
